<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:course xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="MACS 100" href="schedule/2018/fall/MACS/100.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2018" href="schedule/2018.xml">2018</calendarYear><term id="120188" href="schedule/2018/fall.xml">Fall 2018</term><subject id="MACS" href="schedule/2018/fall/MACS.xml">Media and Cinema Studies</subject></parents><label>Intro to Popular TV &amp; Movies</label><description>The goal of this course is for students to begin to develop a critical understanding of the role of popular movies and television in their own lives and in U.S. culture.  The course looks at issues of the relationship of media to social violence, gender identities, sexual identities, adolescents, minority cultures, and the role of the U.S. media globally. It also considers some of the major media genres that characterize U.S. popular television and movies.</description><creditHours>3 hours.</creditHours><sectionDegreeAttributes>Humanities - Lit &amp; Arts, and Cultural Studies - Western course.</sectionDegreeAttributes><genEdCategories><category id="CS"><description>Cultural Studies</description><ns2:genEdAttributes><genEdAttribute code="1WCC">Cultural Studies - Western</genEdAttribute></ns2:genEdAttributes></category><category id="HUM"><description>Humanities &amp; the Arts</description><ns2:genEdAttributes><genEdAttribute code="1LA">Humanities – Lit &amp; Arts</genEdAttribute></ns2:genEdAttributes></category></genEdCategories><sections><section id="66220" href="schedule/2018/fall/MACS/100/66220.xml">AD2</section><section id="66221" href="schedule/2018/fall/MACS/100/66221.xml">AD3</section><section id="66222" href="schedule/2018/fall/MACS/100/66222.xml">AD4</section><section id="66223" href="schedule/2018/fall/MACS/100/66223.xml">AD5</section><section id="66224" href="schedule/2018/fall/MACS/100/66224.xml">AD6</section><section id="66226" href="schedule/2018/fall/MACS/100/66226.xml">AD7</section><section id="66225